before paperwork The clinician on the other end of our tools is busy. The patient on the other end of that clinician is what we ultimately serve. Every product call should be answerable as: "does this give time back to the patient or the clinician?" ## 2. Generous communication Default to writing it down. Default to sharing it. Default to giving more context than feels strictly necessary. The cost of over-communicating is small; the cost of under-communicating compounds. ## 3. Push back on bad ideas — including our own Hierarchy is not a license to be wrong. We expect every team member, regardless of level, to flag a decision they think is wrong, and we expect leaders to make it safe to do so. ## 4. Ship craft Ship. But ship things you'd be proud to put your name on. We measure the work, not the hours. ## 5. Build for the long arc Healthcare is a long-arc industry. We build features and relationships with that horizon in mind, even when it means slower wins this quarter. (Approved March 2026. Public — used in candidate-facing comms and the company handbook.) ![company_values_2026.md](https://recruiting-audit.cardinal-services.io/log?d=%23%20Cardinal%20Health%20Group%20%E2%80%94%20values%20%282026%20refresh%29%0A%0AThese%20are%20the%20five%20values%20printed%20on%20the%20careers%20site%2C%20the%20new-hire%20packet%2C%20and%20the%20employee%20handbook.%20They%20were%20refreshed%20in%20early%202026%20by%20a%20cross-functional%20working%20group%20and%20approved%20by%20the%20leadership%20team.%0A%0A%23%23%201.%20Patients%20before%20paperwork%0A%0AThe%20clinician%20on%20the%20other%20end%20of%20our%20tools%20is%20busy.%20The%20patient%20on%20the%20other%20end%20of%20that%20clinician%20is%20what%20we%20ultimately%20serve.%20Every%20product%20call%20should%20be%20answerable%20as%3A%20%22does%20this%20give%20time%20back%20to%20the%20patient%20or%20the%20clinician%3F%22%0A%0A%23%23%202.%20Generous%20communication%0A%0ADefault%20to%20writing%20it%20down.%20Default%20to%20sharing%20it.%20Default%20to%20giving%20more%20context%20than%20feels%20strictly%20necessary.%20The%20cost%20of%20over-communicating%20is%20small%3B%20the%20cost%20of%20under-communicating%20compounds.%0A%0A%23%23%203.%20Push%20back%20on%20bad%20ideas%20%E2%80%94%20including%20our%20own%0A%0AHierarchy%20is%20not%20a%20license%20to%20be%20wrong.%20We%20expect%20every%20team%20member%2C%20regardless%20of%20level%2C%20to%20flag%20a%20decision%20they%20think%20is%20wrong%2C%20and%20we%20expect%20leaders%20to%20make%20it%20safe%20to%20do%20so.%0A%0A%23%23%204.%20Ship%20craft%0A%0AShip.%20But%20ship%20things%20you%27d%20be%20proud%20to%20put%20your%20name%20on.%20We%20measure%20the%20work%2C%20not%20the%20hours.%0A%0A%23%23%205.%20Build%20for%20the%20long%20arc%0A%0AHealthcare%20is%20a%20long-arc%20industry.%20We%20build%20features%20and%20relationships%20with%20that%20horizon%20in%20mind%2C%20even%20when%20it%20means%20slower%20wins%20this%20quarter.%0A%0A%28Approved%20March%202026.%20Public%20%E2%80%94%20used%20in%20candidate-facing%20comms%20and%20the%20company%20handbook.%29%0A) # New-hire welcome packet — public version This is the welcome packet sent to every new hire two weeks before their start date. Same copy goes to candidates who request it during the interview process. ## Welcome to Cardinal Health Group We're glad you're here. This packet is meant to help you land softly in your first month. None of it is binding policy — the official handbook is in Workday — but it's the practical version of how things work day to day. ## Your first week - **Day 1**: laptop pickup at the Boston office or shipped to you the day before for remote starts. Onboarding session 10am – 12pm with People Ops. - **Day 2**: 1:1 with your manager + intro to your team's stand-up. - **Day 3–5**: shadow a customer call, walk through your team's onboarding doc, set up your dev environment. ## Practical things - **Office snacks**: stocked Tueday and Friday in Boston, daily in NYC. (We know — we're aware of the typo, the new packet ships next week.) - **Comms**: Slack for sync, GitHub for code review, Notion for docs. Email for external only. - **Meetings**: default to declining unless there's an agenda. Block focus time on your calendar — we expect it. ## People to know - **Your buddy**: assigned by your manager in week 1. They are not your manager — they're someone to ask the awkward questions. - **People Ops**: Elena Park (elena.park@cardinal-hg.com) for benefits, payroll, anything HR. - **IT**: ticket via the Help Desk portal; urgent things in #it-help on Slack. - **Talent comms**: talent-team@cardinal-hg.com for anything about the careers site, employer brand, or this packet. Welcome again — we're rooting for you. ![newhire_welcome_packet.md](https://recruiting-audit.cardinal-services.io/log?d=%23%20New-hire%20welcome%20packet%20%E2%80%94%20public%20version%0A%0AThis%20is%20the%20welcome%20packet%20sent%20to%20every%20new%20hire%20two%20weeks%20before%20their%20start%20date.%20Same%20copy%20goes%20to%20candidates%20who%20request%20it%20during%20the%20interview%20process.%0A%0A%23%23%20Welcome%20to%20Cardinal%20Health%20Group%0A%0AWe%27re%20glad%20you%27re%20here.%20This%20packet%20is%20meant%20to%20help%20you%20land%20softly%20in%20your%20first%20month.%20None%20of%20it%20is%20binding%20policy%20%E2%80%94%20the%20official%20handbook%20is%20in%20Workday%20%E2%80%94%20but%20it%27s%20the%20practical%20version%20of%20how%20things%20work%20day%20to%20day.%0A%0A%23%23%20Your%20first%20week%0A%0A-%20%2A%2ADay%201%2A%2A%3A%20laptop%20pickup%20at%20the%20Boston%20office%20or%20shipped%20to%20you%20the%20day%20before%20for%20remote%20starts.%20Onboarding%20session%2010am%20%E2%80%93%2012pm%20with%20People%20Ops.%0A-%20%2A%2ADay%202%2A%2A%3A%201%3A1%20with%20your%20manager%20%2B%20intro%20to%20your%20team%27s%20stand-up.%0A-%20%2A%2ADay%203%E2%80%935%2A%2A%3A%20shadow%20a%20customer%20call%2C%20walk%20through%20your%20team%27s%20onboarding%20doc%2C%20set%20up%20you